course: dictionary
lesson: 2872
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «dong» is one of them. Context tells you which meaning is right. Read the words around the word first: the clues in the sentence show you what it means.
explain: «You probably know a Ukrainian song already: "Carol of the Bells", the ding-ding-dong Christmas tune.» The words ding-ding and Christmas tune are the clues. Dong is the deep ringing sound of a large bell. Swap that meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Now look at «The dong is the money of Vietnam.» The words money and Vietnam are the clues, so here dong is a currency, the money people use there. If a sentence talks about bells or ringing, choose the sound meaning. If it talks about money or a country, choose the money meaning.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is a useful kind of word to watch out for.
fact: «Dong» means the deep ringing sound of a large bell.
fact: «Dong» also means the money of Vietnam.
fact: «Ding-dong» is a sound word, like the ringing of a bell.
fact: As a noun, dong has the plural dongs; as a verb it is rare.
exercise: «You probably know a Ukrainian song already: "Carol of the Bells", the ding-ding-dong Christmas tune.» What does dong mean in this sentence? | *The deep ringing sound of a large bell | A type of Ukrainian dance | The money of Vietnam | A kind of sweet
exercise: In «The dong is the money of Vietnam», which word tells you that dong means money? | *money | the | is | dong
exercise: In the phrase «the bell went dong», what does dong describe? | *A deep ringing sound | A quiet tap of feet | A loud splash in water | A high squeak
test: Which meaning fits «ding-dong» in a story about a church tower? | A Christmas present | A kind of sweet | The money of Vietnam | *The ringing sound of a large bell
test: What is the dong? | A type of bell tower | *The money of Vietnam | A Ukrainian song | A bird that sings at dawn
exam: Two sentences use dong: one about a bell, one about a price in Vietnam. What do the clues tell you each time? | The clues are the same, so either meaning works | The word is always a verb | *Bell sounds point to the ringing meaning; Vietnam and price point to the money meaning | Dong always means money
